          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Expected behavior\n\n- **Collections/min** measures how often the exporter refreshes data from Slurm. The default 30s interval is approximately 2/min.\n- **Metrics requests/min** measures how often Prometheus scrapes the business-metrics endpoint. The exporter is pull-based and does not send metrics itself.\n- Cadence should be flat. Compare collection duration with the inferred interval and collection-loop utilization to find loss of headroom.\n- Collector errors do not remove the other collectors' data. The failed collector retains its last successful data until recovery.\n- Skipped runs mean the previous run is still in flight. Correlate skips with collector duration and inflight concurrency.\n- A sudden drop in exported samples can indicate incomplete Slurm data even when the endpoint remains UP.\n\nThe current metric set does not expose the timestamp of the last successful collection. Exact data age cannot be calculated; cadence and gaps are inferred from counter rates.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
